        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benjamin Britten, Béla Bartók, Paul Arma\n- Works: War Requiem, Suite Paysanne Hongroise\n- Roles: composer, conductor, pianist, ethnomusicologist\n- Topics: English music, Hungarian music, musical arrangement\n\nFacts:\n- Béla Bartók was born on 25 March 1881 and died on 26 September 1945.\n- Béla Bartók was a Hungarian composer, pianist, and ethnomusicologist.\n- Benjamin Britten, Baron Britten, was born on 22 November 1913 and died on 4 December 1976.\n- Benjamin Britten was an English composer, conductor, and pianist.\n- War Requiem is identified as an opus work titled War Requiem.\n- Suite Paysanne Hongroise is an arrangement of music by Béla Bartók.\n- Paul Arma made the arrangement titled Suite Paysanne Hongroise.",
